          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              What is the difference between mattress cleaning and mattress sanitation?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              <strong>Cleaning</strong> can mean anything from spot treatment to wet extraction, so ask any provider what equipment they use and how much water goes in. <strong>Sanitation</strong>, as we do it, is a disciplined protocol that treats the mattress as a sleep environment: controlled dry vapor steam, low-moisture discipline, and attention to seams, tufts and edges. If you want the whole sleep surface treated, not just visible stains, that is what sanitation covers.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              How long will my mattress take to dry after service?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              Dry vapor steam puts far less liquid water into a mattress than hot-water extraction, so there is less to dry. Humidity, mattress thickness and bedroom airflow all change the time, and we tell you what to expect for your bed at the visit. Sleep Sanitation's guide to <a href="https://sleepsanitation.com/knowledge-center/mattress-moisture-heat-drying-construction/how-quickly-should-a-treated-mattress-dry" style="color:var(--charcoal); font-weight:600; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">how quickly a treated mattress should dry</a> has the detail.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              Can you treat memory foam, latex and hybrid mattresses?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              Yes. Memory foam and latex are sensitive to soaking, which is why we avoid high-moisture extraction. We inspect the fabric and construction first and set steam temperature and pass speed for that material. Your care label and warranty terms still come first, so check them before booking.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              What does your price cover?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              Our first mattress is $249, with normal stains, pet odor and ordinary urine accidents included ($199 during our Fall 2026 promotion). We arrive with a sleep-surface protocol, dedicated dry vapor steam equipment, and a white-glove entry standard. You are paying for an appointment that is only about your mattress.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              Do I need to strip the bed and move furniture before you arrive?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              We ask that linens and mattress protectors be removed so we can assess and treat the full sleep surface. If you need assistance with this, mention it when booking and our technician will help as part of the clean-entry protocol. We handle light furniture repositioning around the bed, but we do not require you to move heavy dressers or nightstands.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details style="background:var(--white); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:var(--radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow); overflow:hidden;">
            <summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:1.2rem 1.4rem; font-weight:600; font-size:1.02rem; position:relative; color:var(--charcoal);">
              Do you treat bed mites?
              <span style="position:absolute; right:1.3rem; top:50%; transform:translateY(-50%); color:var(--gold-dark); font-size:1.3rem;">+</span>
            </summary>
            <div style="padding: 0 1.4rem 1.3rem; color:var(--stone); font-size:0.98rem; line-height:1.6;">
              Yes. Bed mites (house dust mites) live in the dust and shed skin flakes that collect in seams, tufts and edges, and our dry vapor steam uses heat to kill them there. Published steam tests back the heat effect: Glass and Needham (2004) reported 100 percent mortality of D. farinae after a 96°C steam cleaner on carpet and mattress samples, and Colloff and colleagues (1995) found no live mites in steamed, lab-seeded carpet squares over four months. Those were study conditions, not your bedroom. Dead mites and droppings still need removing, so we HEPA vacuum too. We make no allergy or asthma claim. Sleep Sanitation's <a href="https://sleepsanitation.com/knowledge-center/mattress-dust-mites-allergens/does-steam-kill-dust-mites-in-mattresses" style="color:var(--charcoal); font-weight:600; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px;">steam and bed mite review</a> covers both studies. <em>General information, not medical advice.</em>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
